WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.550 --> 00:00:07.100
Varys: The Maesters tell us that Aegon came
to Westeros with fire and blood, and hammered

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:09.300
six kingdoms into one.

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:15.559
The fire he undoubtedly brought, as the Kings
of the Rock, Reach, and Iron Islands learned.

00:00:15.559 --> 00:00:21.490
Aegon's own son, Maegor the Cruel, was killed
by the very Iron Throne his father had forged

00:00:21.490 --> 00:00:23.670
if you believe the tales.

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:28.660
If you don't, then perhaps "the Cruel" is
not a wise name for a king to earn.

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:33.750
Daeron, First of His Name, tried to finish
his ancestors' work and bring Dorne into the

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:34.750
fold.

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:41.280
For his efforts, he lost sixty thousand men
and his own life of eighteen years.

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:46.230
During the great Targaryen civil war known
as "the Dance of the Dragons," a king and

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:52.160
queen each vied for the throne, dividing their
house and its dragons against each other.

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:57.220
Eventually, the queen was fed to her rival's
dragon while her son watched, and the victorious

00:00:57.220 --> 00:01:00.200
king soon died of his own wounds.

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:06.100
By the war's end, King's Landing was smashed,
cities razed and sacked never to be rebuilt,

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:17.170
and dragons had faded from this world.

00:01:17.170 --> 00:01:47.850
Jaime Lannister: For centuries, the Kingsguard
have been the 

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:59.240
glory 
of the realm.

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:03.680
Aegon the Conqueror had established the order
as his personal guardians after uniting Westeros

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:05.460
with fire and blood.

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:09.670
He knew that some of his subjects wouldn't
take to conquest, and his dragons were no

00:02:09.670 --> 00:02:12.099
use against knives in the dark.

00:02:12.099 --> 00:02:16.780
No doubt surrounding himself with the greatest
knights in Westeros made his rule more palatable

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:19.910
and less foreign as well.

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:23.640
Everyone in his kingdoms soon knew the names
and some of the songs of the Kingsguard.

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:26.349
I certainly did from earliest days.

00:02:26.349 --> 00:02:31.180
Bronn: There was one Kingsguard (I forgot
the bastard's name) who swore an oath to his

00:02:31.180 --> 00:02:34.860
dying Targaryen king to crown his daughter
after him.

00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:39.620
The very night that king died, this Kingsguard
crowned the king's son instead.

00:02:39.620 --> 00:02:44.010
When an old man on the Small Council dared
to protest, this honorable knight opened his

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:45.010
throat.

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:49.790
The bastard died in the very civil war he
started along with the old king's son, daughter,

00:02:49.790 --> 00:02:51.260
and most of their dragons.

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:53.210
And the Kingsguard?

00:02:53.210 --> 00:02:58.690
All that duty and honor and not enough brains
to figure out which Targaryen to give it to.

00:02:58.690 --> 00:03:03.500
Twin brothers even ended up on opposite sides,
died with tears on their cheeks as they cut

00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:04.510
each other down.

00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:09.849
I suppose I should think that's tragic, but
stupid men do stupid things every day and

00:03:09.849 --> 00:03:11.269
nobody cries over them.

00:03:11.269 --> 00:03:15.409
Petyr Baelish: As little more than a boy,
Ser Criston Cole replaced the legendary Ser

00:03:15.409 --> 00:03:19.510
Ryam Redwyne on the Kingsguard and soon rose
to Lord Commander.

00:03:19.510 --> 00:03:22.849
But knights only know one way to settle disputes.

00:03:22.849 --> 00:03:27.159
When Prince Aegon's father died, Ser Criston
slit the throat of an advisor who objected

00:03:27.159 --> 00:03:30.580
to Aegon's ascension over his aunt, the anointed
heir.

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:35.360
His actions so pleased the new King, Aegon,
Second of His Name, that he appointed Ser

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:40.170
Criston as his Hand in the ensuing civil war
called the Dance of Dragons.

00:03:40.170 --> 00:03:45.700
Neither Ser Criston nor the King nor even
the Targaryen dragons would survive it.

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:50.909
Viserys Targaryen: The Targaryen dynasty united
the Seven Kingdoms and lasted nearly three

00:03:50.909 --> 00:03:51.909
centuries.

00:03:51.909 --> 00:03:59.920
It was a dynasty forged in fire, sealed in
blood, and destroyed by rebellion.

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:05.709
The Targaryens are blood of the dragon, descended
from the nobility of ancient Valyria, a once-mighty

00:04:05.709 --> 00:04:07.710
empire in the east.

00:04:07.710 --> 00:04:13.849
When the cataclysmic Doom laid waste of Valyria
and its people, the Targaryens survived, having

00:04:13.849 --> 00:04:17.080
settled in the island fortress of Dragonstone
years before.

00:04:17.080 --> 00:04:23.910
They remained there for a century until the
rise of Aegon the Conqueror.

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:29.800
Instead of attempting to reclaim the eastern
lands of his ancestors, Aegon sailed west

00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:36.210
for the Seven Kingdoms, his sisters Visenya
and Rhaenys at his side.

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:41.570
To keep the bloodlines pure, Aegon continued
the custom of his Valyrian ancestors and took

00:04:41.570 --> 00:04:44.220
both of his sisters to wives.

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:48.419
Together, they came ashore on the eastern
coast of Westeros.

00:04:48.419 --> 00:04:53.880
Their blazon: a dragon with three heads, representing
Aegon and his sister-wives.

00:04:53.880 --> 00:04:59.900
Their words: "Fire and Blood."

00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:05.630
While their host was small when compared to
the armies of the Seven Kingdoms, Aegon and

00:05:05.630 --> 00:05:08.790
his sisters had a secret weapon.

00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:11.820
The last of the dragons.

00:05:11.820 --> 00:05:17.259
He conquered every kingdom, save Dorne, which
eventually bowed to Targaryen rule a century

00:05:17.259 --> 00:05:18.259
later.

00:05:18.259 --> 00:05:23.410
He had the swords of his enemies melted down
by the fiery breath of his dragon, Balerion

00:05:23.410 --> 00:05:29.000
the Black Dread, and forged into the Iron
Throne.

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:33.850
The capital city of King's Landing was built
on the eastern coast, where Aegon and his

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:35.380
sisters first came ashore.

00:05:35.380 --> 00:05:41.530
And Aegon ordered the construction of a royal
castle on its highest hill, the Red Keep.

00:05:41.530 --> 00:05:46.740
Joffrey Baratheon: Aegon built his castle
of red rock to remind people of the fires

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:52.150
he had roasted his enemies in, so whenever
King's Landing looked up, they'd see the price

00:05:52.150 --> 00:05:54.280
of defiance.

00:05:54.280 --> 00:05:57.470
He knew the first rule of kings.

00:05:57.470 --> 00:06:01.210
Only fear keeps men in line.

00:06:01.210 --> 00:06:03.350
Fear and punishment.

00:06:03.350 --> 00:06:10.380
Then again, torture chambers are just so private.

00:06:10.380 --> 00:06:15.670
Better to punish your enemies where everyone
can see and remember.

00:06:15.670 --> 00:06:21.479
Like that Targaryen who forced his nephew
to watch as he fed the boy's traitor mother

00:06:21.479 --> 00:06:22.509
to a dragon.

00:06:22.509 --> 00:06:25.590
Oh, what I could do with a dragon.

00:06:25.590 --> 00:06:31.780
Euron Greyjoy: The stories claimed that the
Old Way died with Harren the Black and his

00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:33.150
sons in Harrenhal.

00:06:33.150 --> 00:06:39.030
Our ships and axes were no match for Aegon's
dragons, so our ancestors bent their steel

00:06:39.030 --> 00:06:45.160
into fishhooks and our kingdom into villages
and started telling the red tales around the

00:06:45.160 --> 00:06:51.520
fire of how we used to be strong and how one
day we would be so again.

00:06:51.520 --> 00:06:54.930
Generations later, a young boy listened to
them.

00:06:54.930 --> 00:07:01.879
Dalton Greyjoy, the wild young heir to Pyke,
was rowing at five and reaving at ten in the

00:07:01.879 --> 00:07:04.120
Basilisk Isles with his uncle.

00:07:04.120 --> 00:07:11.530
By fourteen, Dalton had sailed as far as Old
Ghis, fought in a dozen battles, and claimed

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:12.900
four salt wives.

00:07:12.900 --> 00:07:19.300
In his fifteenth year, he avenged his uncle's
death in battle, but he took a dozen wounds

00:07:19.300 --> 00:07:23.889
and emerged from the fight drenched head to
heel in blood.

00:07:23.889 --> 00:07:30.030
From that day forth, men called him the Red
Kraken.

00:07:30.030 --> 00:07:35.770
During the Dance of Dragons, the Red Kraken
picked the side that was fighting the Lannisters

00:07:35.770 --> 00:07:39.990
and fell upon the Westerlands while the Lannisters
were off at war.

00:07:39.990 --> 00:07:46.321
Casterly Rock itself proved too strong once
the lady of the castle barred its gates, but

00:07:46.321 --> 00:07:52.720
the ironborn burned the Lannister fleet and
sacked Lannisport carrying off gold, grain,

00:07:52.720 --> 00:07:57.900
and hundreds of women and girls, including
Lord Lannister's favorite mistress and all

00:07:57.900 --> 00:07:59.780
his bastards.

00:07:59.780 --> 00:08:05.940
The Red Kraken now ruled the Sunset Sea as
his forbears had, and his longships again

00:08:05.940 --> 00:08:08.590
brought the Old Way to the coast of Westeros.

00:08:08.590 --> 00:08:14.050
But then the war ended, and the mainland armies
came home.

00:08:14.050 --> 00:08:20.379
The Iron Throne commanded the Red Kraken to
stop reaving, and when he didn't, a mistress

00:08:20.379 --> 00:08:23.030
opened his throat as he slept.

00:08:23.030 --> 00:08:29.680
While his sons squabbled, the Lannisters sent
their soldiers to the Iron Islands.

00:08:29.680 --> 00:08:35.070
Thousands of men, women, and children were
put to the sword, and scores of villages and

00:08:35.070 --> 00:08:38.519
hundreds of longships were put to the torch.

00:08:38.519 --> 00:08:44.590
The glorious return to the Old Way had lasted
almost two years.

00:08:44.590 --> 00:08:50.010
Varys: In its time, the Dragonpit was a marvel
of the world.

00:08:50.010 --> 00:08:56.130
Full-grown Targaryen dragons nested beneath
its massive dome, and even on the darkest

00:08:56.130 --> 00:09:00.940
nights, the walls seemed to glow with the
fire of the great beasts inside.

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:08.720
Qyburn: As had the site's previous occupant,
the Sept of Remembrance, when Maegor the Cruel

00:09:08.720 --> 00:09:11.550
blasted it with dragonfire during morning
prayers.

00:09:11.550 --> 00:09:17.269
The screams of the dying men echoed through
King's Landing all day, and a pall of ash

00:09:17.269 --> 00:09:20.149
and smoke hung over the city for a week.

00:09:20.149 --> 00:09:26.100
Varys: But as it dissipated, so too did the
rebellion of the Faith Militant.

00:09:26.100 --> 00:09:32.149
The Sept of Remembrance faded from memory,
and Maegor decided to replace a monument to

00:09:32.149 --> 00:09:36.880
the gods with a monument to his family: the
Dragonpit.

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:43.470
Qyburn: Labor proved elusive, however, for
after the Red Keep was finished, Maegor had

00:09:43.470 --> 00:09:48.710
hosted a three-day feast for all builders,
stonemasons, and carpenters who had worked

00:09:48.710 --> 00:09:50.050
to build it.

00:09:50.050 --> 00:09:56.250
At its conclusion, he slaughtered them, so
that only he would know the castle's secrets.

00:09:56.250 --> 00:10:01.470
So many men fled the construction of the Dragonpit
that Maegor was forced to employ the prisoners

00:10:01.470 --> 00:10:07.279
of the city dungeons, supplemented by skilled
and ignorant builders from across the Narrow

00:10:07.279 --> 00:10:08.350
Sea.

00:10:08.350 --> 00:10:14.551
Varys: For more than a century, the Targaryens
housed their dragons in the Dragonpit.

00:10:14.551 --> 00:10:18.540
But dragons are not horsesto be stabled or
hounds to be kenneled.

00:10:18.540 --> 00:10:23.290
With each generation, the dragons became less.

00:10:23.290 --> 00:10:26.950
Less massive, less swift, less long-lived.

00:10:26.950 --> 00:10:31.440
Qyburn: And less invulnerable.

00:10:31.440 --> 00:10:36.530
During the Dance of Dragons, two Targaryen
factions killed a handful of their family's

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:39.060
dragons while fighting each other.

00:10:39.060 --> 00:10:44.940
A frenzied mob even broke into the Dragonpit
and slaughtered the five dragons chained there,

00:10:44.940 --> 00:10:50.610
though the last managed to bring down the
roof of the great dome on its assailants.

00:10:50.610 --> 00:10:55.760
The dragons never recovered their former strength
or numbers.

00:10:55.760 --> 00:11:03.750
Perhaps their line had been too broken, or
perhaps others intervened to break it further.

00:11:03.750 --> 00:11:25.839
But the last dragon grew no larger than a
cat, and its death earned Aegon, Third of

00:11:25.839 --> 00:11:40.700
His Name, the epithet "Dragonbane."

